{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/446422-weakening-strengthing-2nd-ed-pack-totems-and-the-others","id":446422,"title":"Weakening/Strengthing 2nd Ed Pack Totems, and the Others","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-17T13:20:16-07:00","id":446422,"title":"Weakening/Strengthing 2nd Ed Pack Totems, and the Others","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I was reviewing the Totem rules and I was wondering. During play, if all the Werewolves in the pack (let's go with three) have maxed out the Totem Merits, and they've all created one Wolf-Blooded. That would leave them with 18 Totem Points, could they during play, recruit Wolf-Blooded and bring them into the pack to increase their Totem points? If this is possible would this just &quot;happen&quot; or would there need to be an initiation Rite?<br /> <br /> Also could the reverse be true? Could they weaken the Totem of a rival pack by killing off wolf-blooded and individual werewolves? I'm in particular thinking of the powerful Pure Totems.<br /> <br /> And finally how would you guys handle having other Supernaturals in the Pack? The Sidebar on pg. 90, suggests treating them as supporting wolf-blooded, so granting the pack with 1 Totem Point. I'm think of only letting entities with Spiritual ties, like the Dead Wolves Bloodline, Vampires with Blood Teneborous, Spirit Mages, Ulgan Prometheans or beings with other Spiritual powers join the pack at that level or higher, I'm thinking of even letting them potentially purchase the Pack Bond Merit. While those without Spiritual ties or abilities being stuck in the Periphery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T15:12:06-07:00","id":446595,"title":"","content":"There doesn't seem to be an initiation rite, it does seem like <i>something</i> happens. Maybe it's just letting them know the truth about things, maybe it's a big formal trial. I'd probably have established packs have a makeshift rite for it but otherwise it's the kind of thing that when you're in you're in.<br /> <br /> Regarding weakening the totem, I think it would be a perfectly valid way to do so, killing members with totem points. Or you could kill a totem and suddenly members of its pack lose the bonuses it granted them.<br /> <br /> That sounds right with the supernatural members. They shouldn't be fitted in like humans, since they're likely to know more about the wolf-blooded level workings of things, rather than be almost oblivious as some humans are. Everyone's going to want their own thing with that, whether it's just banning the rule or requiring them to join on the hunt, ideally the crunch of that will stay on a table-by-table basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-17-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:00:42-07:00","id":446636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/446422-weakening-strengthing-2nd-ed-pack-totems-and-the-others?p=446595#post446595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn't seem to be an initiation rite, it does seem like <i>something</i> happens. Maybe it's just letting them know the truth about things, maybe it's a big formal trial. I'd probably have established packs have a makeshift rite for it but otherwise it's the kind of thing that when you're in you're in.<br /> <br /> Regarding weakening the totem, I think it would be a perfectly valid way to do so, killing members with totem points. Or you could kill a totem and suddenly members of its pack lose the bonuses it granted them.<br /> <br /> That sounds right with the supernatural members. They shouldn't be fitted in like humans, since they're likely to know more about the wolf-blooded level workings of things, rather than be almost oblivious as some humans are. Everyone's going to want their own thing with that, whether it's just banning the rule or requiring them to join on the hunt, ideally the crunch of that will stay on a table-by-table basis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome! I think I'm going with a informal &quot;Rite&quot; (no Experience required) and let the pack grow that way. And has for &quot;balance&quot; their Totem can be weakened just like any other.<br /> <br /> As for Supernaturals thanks! So what'll I'll be going with is; Supernaturals are naturally at the Wolf-Blooded level, even those without Spiritual abilities. While leaving the possibility open for Spiritually &quot;attuned&quot; creatures capable of proving themselves to be able of holding their own on the Siskur-Dah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}